usb: complete the EP0 control transfer when stalling it

usbd_ep_set_stall() only set USB_CX_STL for EP0. After the stack stalls an
OUT control request (with or without a data stage), the controller ignores
every following control transfer until the next bus reset; IN requests are
not affected. Setting USB_CX_DONE in the same register write as USB_CX_STL
lets the next SETUP be handled; the lhal maintainer requires the two bits in
one write (review of patch set 1). Measured on BL616CL with CherryUSB CDC ACM
(Linux host, usbfs): without this change EP0 stops after the first stalled
vendor OUT request; with it 50 of 50 rounds recover for each of five kinds of
stalled request.

Applies to drivers/lhal/src/bflb_usb_v2.c of bouffalo_sdk v2.3.37
(identical to lhal master 911501a).
Upstream review: https://gerrit.bouffalolab.com/c/bouffalo/drivers/lhal/+/11805 (patch set 2)
Drop this patch when sources.json moves to an SDK release that contains it.

--- a/drivers/lhal/src/bflb_usb_v2.c
+++ b/drivers/lhal/src/bflb_usb_v2.c
@@ -1195,8 +1195,11 @@ int usbd_ep_set_stall(uint8_t busid, const uint8_t ep)
     uint8_t ep_idx = USB_EP_GET_IDX(ep);
 
     if (ep_idx == 0) {
+        /* Set CX_DONE in the same write as CX_STL to also complete the control
+         * transfer. Otherwise, after an OUT request is stalled, the controller
+         * ignores every following control transfer until the next bus reset. */
         regval = getreg32(BFLB_USB_BASE + USB_DEV_CXCFE_OFFSET);
-        regval |= USB_CX_STL;
+        regval |= USB_CX_STL | USB_CX_DONE;
         putreg32(regval, BFLB_USB_BASE + USB_DEV_CXCFE_OFFSET);
     } else {
         if (USB_EP_DIR_IS_OUT(ep)) {
